      {
        "id": 113061,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-12T02:26:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Absolution doesn't have to be for something she's done, it could be for her perception of herself.</p><p>Fanatic knew whe was different, and thought she would be hunted for it. &nbsp;It could be that she grew up in a harsh environment and her fight against evil could be a search for Absolution for herself, from what she is, or from perceived faults that she can't control.</p><p>Many unstable minds (and stable ones too) see in themselves all sorts of faults that may or may not exist but are perceived as terrible unforgivable things.</p><p>Give Fanatic a harsh upbringing with a heavy sense of obligation given that her life was spared, and a penchant for instability we see (at least in her early career) and I think it is possible that Absolution is her sword and her quest, to try and earn approval and forgiveness.</p>",
        "post_number": 72,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:44:33.770Z",
